      "repair_reason": "- [P2] The remaining blocker is a narrow parser/test repair that does not require product direction, though the protected maintainer label still means humans decide whether to run automation.; Needs attention: The diff improves the exec approval boundary, but the remaining pnpm shorthand path is a concrete durable-approval bypass risk.; Review finding: [P1] Fail closed pnpm implicit exec shorthands — src/infra/packa... (sha=86c74349aa760f8e30fe7ad6ba47e3702253c22a)",
      "review_summary": "The PR adds shared package-manager exec parsing and wires allowlist matching, allow-always persistence, tests, and node-host mutable operand binding to target inner package-manager commands.\n\nPR surface: Source +279, Tests +848. Total +1127 across 10 files.\n\nReproducibility: yes. Source inspection gives a high-confidence reproduction path: `pnpm eslint .` falls through as `not-exec`, so the normal executable allowlist path can still match a stale resolved `pnpm` entry.",
